  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Highway, Street, and Bridge Construction (NAICS 237310) has $1.9B in federal contract obligations for FY2026 to date. Total award activity includes 1,781 awards and an average award size of $1.1M. Obligations are up 59.7% year over year. The Department of Transportation is the largest buyer, with $716M obligated, followed by the Department of Defense with $588M and the Department of Agriculture with $473M. KIEWIT INFRASTRUCTURE SOUTH CO leads vendors with $297M in obligations, followed by AMRIZE SOUTHWEST INC with $96.4M and BFBC LLC with $86.3M. Fiscal-year comparisons show FY26 to date at $1.9B versus FY25 at $1.2B and FY24 at $2.6B. Contracting activity to date reflects a concentrated set of buyers and vendors: the top three buyers account for a substantial share of obligations, and the top vendors hold several large awards. This snapshot covers fiscal year to date totals and partial-year activity, not full-year final figures.",
    "sections": [
